From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] style(fusion): drop 2362 blank lines the port inserted after
 every line

The TurboQuant port emitted every line of these five files followed by an empty
line, which doubled their length without changing a single statement:

  ggml/src/CMakeLists.txt            632 -> 1265 lines (real additions: 2)
  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/CMakeLists.txt  281 ->  581 lines (real additions: 21)
  ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt   153 ->  323 lines (real additions: 20)
  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/convert.cu      822 -> 1645 lines (real additions: 2)
  ggml/src/ggml-cuda/dequantize.cuh  481 ->  978 lines (real additions: 17)

The port spliced its own lines in without that trailing blank, which breaks a
naive odd/even split, so the rebuild aligned the non-blank line sequences against
the pristine 9a9394a version and replayed only the real insertions. Checked before
writing: the non-blank line sequence of every rebuilt file is identical to what it
was, so no statement could be lost or reordered.

The real additions are preserved in full:
  CMakeLists   ggml-turbo-quant.c in the ggml-base sources, turbo FA vec instances
  convert.cu   #include "turbo-quant.cuh"
  dequantize.cuh  dequantize_turbo3_0 / dequantize_turbo4_0

Verified after the change:
  BUILD_OK
  ggml-base.dll still carries the "turbo3"/"turbo4" type names (6 / 4 hits)
  qwen2.5-1.5B q8_0     -> "The capital of France is Paris", 1529.3 / 151.2 t/s
  Ternary-Bonsai PQ2_0  -> 69.2 / 40.9 t/s

That these files are diffable again matters now rather than later: the TurboQuant
cache types are still not usable in this worktree (common/arg.cpp never got the
type names), so this is the first step of completing the fusion.
